# RS1a RED proof — mutation battery transcript

Increment RS1a (data layer) of `2026-10-15-review-screen-batch`. Every named
RS1a mutant is executed RED (mutate → new test FAILS), then the file is
restored and sha256-verified byte-identical, then re-run GREEN. Commands run
one at a time from the worktree root with `-p no:cacheprovider`.

Environment: `env -u NO_COLOR -u TERM`, `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8`.

---

## 1 · M-RS24 — `authors` omitted from `canonical_config`

Product change under test: the `if config.authors:` fold in
`mapper/reqharness/config.py::canonical_config`.

Mutation (position/operation): delete the fold block, leave `return result`.

```text
$ pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_reqharness_registry.py::test_authors_map_changes_config_hash
FAILED tests/test_reqharness_registry.py::test_authors_map_changes_config_hash - assert 'fa46d573…74b' != 'fa46d573…74b'
1 failed in 0.29s
```

Restore: `before=sha256(config.py) after=sha256(config.py)` → `EQUAL`
(restore digest `e7fd2c02092d799f9b03f94191c8d525b8b6e02716ea0d702a2550531a3f3a72`).

```text
$ pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_reqharness_registry.py::test_authors_map_changes_config_hash
1 passed in 0.17s
```

